DEFILE — Firmware Reverse Engineering and Security Analysis

DEFILE is a modified distribution of IFDA (IoT Firmware Deep Analysis), whose
original public source is identified in the supplied project as:
https://github.com/cn0xroot/IFDA

Acknowledgment is retained for the original IFDA project and the authors and
contributors identified by its repository history. Existing copyright notices,
the Apache License 2.0 in LICENSE, and third-party licenses remain applicable.
No transfer of trademark rights or endorsement by upstream contributors is implied.

Significant modifications in this distribution, 2026-11-19:
- Product, Python package, CLI, Go module, progress protocol, configuration
  namespace, executable and documentation identity migrated to DEFILE.
- Product interface and authored documentation converted to native English.
- Legacy data, environment and browser-setting compatibility retained.
- Documentation screenshots rebranded or recaptured.
- Python package data included explicitly in distribution metadata.
- Shared Full/Live workbench styling, static sample adapter, provenance and
  demonstration disclosures, evidence navigation and context restoration added.
- Independent public-source documentation and static deployment configuration
  prepared for the 2026-11-20 release.

Third-party names such as moria, Ghidra, cve-bin-tool, Alpine.js, capstone,
pyelftools, cryptography, Pillow and modernc.org/sqlite retain their own identities.
